{"type":"message","id":"5fc0157c","parentId":"3f0264a3","timestamp":"2026-03-16T11:27:23.457Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0f0f78e1bdd7b2a30169b7e90b07708191a35cbb97c08ba0c5\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpt-kLzfmqw2cvB37jZxtJjQnMoK82VLbSMcOXaGBngwyhL-N99iyn5igPSmY7BFZxA5AlEjbn5sPxhI64zuUCD-4JcrxiDzQtS174vmOmUdL845s1tpTN6WnaTtFiB0t6tUumWmenReoHhzKYYQ3UXbwEcL2jHJ-jV9ae0yBYABVO0zKbO6gVj4wrmEH4yF7y_473sTGwIoxXCVFki7-6WNi-k0Lfe6ndwpScnfo5kAVmMYchgtfLXtrCCGdS33oRYM6Rbvuweopf9W-MUZOOiCJz8U6pfZApbbipzUBU5ksf3NcOtRtKKCWKRadSIcg4m48dFpjsV2tKzTRL-Jh-mjQDb8L0IZKKnWmMi0coPR2Pl_b5f3aYsu9YlNZedpEPeRLHj-6eOud8QGPa-gKbKffioiqvwzOidakZ6-imyqcfLYzTuicgNk1nfaq3iMpmRsao715ErxcUqg0H1c0oZCQJuLdj27BYUWHCWr93zqEUY1jjzwuhRaWlPVggqWbriP4gRGKa_2C-mXylucJdXpoCKx5WGOFWQe7aNa2TQ_f1pkXFrcxSybrOA7jVCKqpNWmsU2C-iYfKjhn7OKKEiXsQUkj4aLL47i-O2TZMh_XMDdxN41UmI2jPhAg_7tLMJSRYEt4QOfo_mtfn__Rzi-JbCHG8NSakyuLJ4SYTMpWyGNFtbTAkPJOTxwrHZIfdHkPSN6Ht8D6a9FYA0jNMlwBbAagnCT7u1mvM1NMAsK4P09aeLb-Qom-qMeLYpDRmt7_F0elK83xpAWD6lUdM2fjuXzqi0fYMiryBIy3RZB4oXZcvQR0FS5lT7c7r3ctvs-8JR0RUJMfd2ft0QY721y6xBwH0jAnaXvUQZYjUCXVJPTc=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_h3Ix75ouNqCxUSUWBQ7DWKo7|fc_0f0f78e1bdd7b2a30169b7e90bad148191b27877d045d76a83","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/pipeline-execution/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: pipeline-execution\ndescription: Execute the fixed LoopOrchestra ML prototype-execution pipeline for a user-provided image by first uploading the image through the same upload API pattern used by the kidney cancer detection skill, then injecting the returned remote image path into the provided prototype JSON payload and POSTing it to the prototype execution endpoint. Use when a user asks to run the pipeline-execution prototype, test the Test_kidney_nexus pipeline, or send an image through this specific endpoint-backed ML pipeline.\n---\n\n# Pipeline Execution\n\nExecute the fixed prototype-execution workflow for one user image. Reuse the same upload logic and Telegram user id handling as the kidney cancer detection skill, then send the full prototype payload to the execution endpoint.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Determine the local image to analyze.\n   - Prefer an explicit local file path when one is available.\n   - If no path is provided, use the most recent supported image under `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n3. Upload the image with a `POST multipart/form-data` request to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\n4. Read the upload response JSON and build the new remote `image_path` by concatenating:\n   - `path + filename`\n5. Load `references/prototype_execution_payload.json`.\n6. Replace every `<image_path_here>` placeholder in that JSON template with the uploaded remote image path.\n7. POST the resulting JSON payload to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n8. Return raw response JSON when possible.\n   - Because the output schema is currently unknown, preserve the endpoint response instead of forcing a narrow result shape.\n\n## Fixed request values\n\nKeep these values static:\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\n- Prototype execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n- Payload template file: `references/prototype_execution_payload.json`\n\n## What this skill runs\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\n```\n\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script automatically selects the newest supported image from `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n\n## Upload response handling\n\nGiven an upload response like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"path\": \"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/\",\n  \"filename\": \"9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\",\n  \"column_names\": null\n}\n```\n\nBuild:\n\n```text\nimage_path = \"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\"\n```\n\nUse that full value everywhere the JSON template contains `<image_path_here>`.\n\n## Output contract for now\n\nReturn JSON with this minimal wrapper:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"uploaded_image_path\": \"string\",\n  \"request_endpoint\": \"string\",\n  \"response\": {}\n}\n```\n\nIf the endpoint returns non-JSON, return the response body as a string inside `response_raw` instead.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/pipeline-execution/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: pipeline-execution\\ndescription: Execute the fixed LoopOrchestra ML prototype-execution pipeline for a user-provided image by first uploading the image through the same upload API pattern used by the kidney cancer detection skill, then injecting the returned remote image path into the provided prototype JSON payload and POSTing it to the prototype execution endpoint. Use when a user asks to run the pipeline-execution prototype, test the Test_kidney_nexus pipeline, or send an image through this specific endpoint-backed ML pipeline.\\n---\\n\\n# Pipeline Execution\\n\\nExecute the fixed prototype-execution workflow for one user image. Reuse the same upload logic and Telegram user id handling as the kidney cancer detection skill, then send the full prototype payload to the execution endpoint.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Determine the local image to analyze.\\n   - Prefer an explicit local file path when one is available.\\n   - If no path is provided, use the most recent supported image under `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\\n3. Upload the image with a `POST multipart/form-data` request to:\\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\\n4. Read the upload response JSON and build the new remote `image_path` by concatenating:\\n   - `path + filename`\\n5. Load `references/prototype_execution_payload.json`.\\n6. Replace every `<image_path_here>` placeholder in that JSON template with the uploaded remote image path.\\n7. POST the resulting JSON payload to:\\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\\n8. Return raw response JSON when possible.\\n   - Because the output schema is currently unknown, preserve the endpoint response instead of forcing a narrow result shape.\\n\\n## Fixed request values\\n\\nKeep these values static:\\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\\n- Prototype execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\\n- Payload template file: `references/prototype_execution_payload.json`\\n\\n## What this skill runs\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\\n```\\n\\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script automatically selects the newest supported image from `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\\n\\n## Upload response handling\\n\\nGiven an upload response like:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/\\\",\\n  \\\"filename\\\": \\\"9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\\\",\\n  \\\"column_names\\\": null\\n}\\n```\\n\\nBuild:\\n\\n```text\\nimage_path = \\\"upload/2026-03-15_14.52.42_5EdSbYnzCrKdhainPvGx/9dd106ff-65ad-4a16-a381-6d76e4845c9c.jpg\\\"\\n```\\n\\nUse that full value everywhere the JSON template contains `<image_path_here>`.\\n\\n## Output contract for now\\n\\nReturn JSON with this minimal wrapper:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"uploaded_image_path\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"request_endpoint\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"response\\\": {}\\n}\\n```\\n\\nIf the endpoint returns non-JSON, return the response body as a string inside `response_raw` instead.\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":997,"output":909,"cacheRead":28288,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30194,"cost":{"input":0.0024925000000000004,"output":0.013635,"cacheRead":0.007071999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.023199499999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773660421709}}
{"type":"message","id":"ad5d97f1","parentId":"5fc0157c","timestamp":"2026-03-16T11:27:23.469Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_h3Ix75ouNqCxUSUWBQ7DWKo7|fc_0f0f78e1bdd7b2a30169b7e90bad148191b27877d045d76a83","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 3251 bytes to /home/node/.openclaw/skills/pipeline-execution/SKILL.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773660443464}}
{"type":"message","id":"f18b40c9","parentId":"ad5d97f1","timestamp":"2026-03-16T11:28:09.483Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9mXD1vwr5xlQ1sUW3DuC9huR|fc_0f0f78e1bdd7b2a30169b7e91fc38c8191bc48ff763f36b9a5","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/pipeline-execution/scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport mimetypes\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport uuid\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib import error, parse, request\n\nUPLOAD_BASE_URL = \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload\"\nPIPELINE_EXECUTION_ENDPOINT = (\n    \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/\"\n)\nFIXED_STORAGE_REF = \"nodes_bucket\"\nFIXED_LOCAL_FILE_PATH = \"upload/\"\nSUPPORTED_EXTENSIONS = {\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\", \".webp\", \".gif\", \".bmp\", \".tif\", \".tiff\"}\nSCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nPAYLOAD_TEMPLATE_PATH = SCRIPT_DIR.parent / \"references\" / \"prototype_execution_payload.json\"\nPLACEHOLDER = \"<image_path_here>\"\n\n\ndef _multipart_encode(field_name: str, file_path: Path):\n    boundary = f\"----OpenClawBoundary{uuid.uuid4().hex}\"\n    mime_type = mimetypes.guess_type(file_path.name)[0] or \"application/octet-stream\"\n    file_bytes = file_path.read_bytes()\n\n    parts = [\n        f\"--{boundary}\\r\\n\".encode(\"utf-8\"),\n        (\n            f'Content-Disposition: form-data; name=\"{field_name}\"; '\n            f'filename=\"{file_path.name}\"\\r\\n'\n        ).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n        f\"Content-Type: {mime_type}\\r\\n\\r\\n\".encode(\"utf-8\"),\n        file_bytes,\n        b\"\\r\\n\",\n        f\"--{boundary}--\\r\\n\".encode(\"utf-8\"),\n    ]\n    return boundary, b\"\".join(parts)\n\n\ndef _normalize_upload_response(value):\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        if not value:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Upload response was an empty list.\")\n        first = value[0]\n        if not isinstance(first, dict):\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Upload response list did not contain an object.\")\n        value = first\n\n    if not isinstance(value, dict):\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Upload endpoint returned an unsupported JSON shape.\")\n\n    return value\n\n\ndef upload_image(local_image_path: str, telegram_user_id: str, timeout: int = 60) -> str:\n    file_path = Path(local_image_path).expanduser().resolve()\n    if not file_path.is_file():\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Image file not found: {file_path}\")\n\n    query = parse.urlencode(\n        {\n            \"storage_ref\": FIXED_STORAGE_REF,\n            \"local_file_path\": FIXED_LOCAL_FILE_PATH,\n            \"user_id\": telegram_user_id,\n        }\n    )\n    upload_url = f\"{UPLOAD_BASE_URL}?{query}\"\n    boundary, body = _multipart_encode(\"file\", file_path)\n    req = request.Request(\n        upload_url,\n        data=body,\n        headers={\n            \"Content-Type\": f\"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}\",\n            \"Accept\": \"application/json\",\n        },\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            response_body = resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Upload failed with HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Upload request failed: {e}\") from e\n\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(response_body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Upload endpoint returned a non-JSON response.\") from e\n\n    parsed = _normalize_upload_response(parsed)\n    remote_dir = parsed.get(\"path\")\n    filename = parsed.get(\"filename\")\n    if not isinstance(remote_dir, str) or not remote_dir:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Upload response is missing 'path'.\")\n    if not isinstance(filename, str) or not filename:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Upload response is missing 'filename'.\")\n\n    return f\"{remote_dir}{filename}\"\n\n\ndef find_latest_inbound_image() -> str:\n    inbound_dir = Path(\"/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound\").resolve()\n    if not inbound_dir.is_dir():\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            \"Inbound media directory not found: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound. \"\n            \"Pass --image-path explicitly if the image is stored elsewhere.\"\n        )\n\n    candidates = [\n        path\n        for path in inbound_dir.rglob(\"*\")\n        if path.is_file() and path.suffix.lower() in SUPPORTED_EXTENSIONS\n    ]\n    if not candidates:\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            \"No supported image files found in /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound. \"\n            \"Pass --image-path explicitly if needed.\"\n        )\n\n    latest = max(candidates, key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime)\n    return str(latest)\n\n\ndef load_payload_template() -> dict:\n    if not PAYLOAD_TEMPLATE_PATH.is_file():\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Payload template not found: {PAYLOAD_TEMPLATE_PATH}\")\n\n    try:\n        raw = PAYLOAD_TEMPLATE_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Payload template file is not valid JSON.\") from e\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Payload template must be a JSON object.\")\n\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef inject_image_path(payload: dict, uploaded_image_path: str) -> dict:\n    replaced = json.loads(json.dumps(payload))\n    replaced_json = json.dumps(replaced)\n    if PLACEHOLDER not in replaced_json:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Payload template is missing the placeholder {PLACEHOLDER!r}.\")\n    replaced_json = replaced_json.replace(PLACEHOLDER, uploaded_image_path)\n    return json.loads(replaced_json)\n\n\ndef call_pipeline_execution(payload: dict, timeout: int = 180):\n    body = json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\")\n    req = request.Request(\n        PIPELINE_EXECUTION_ENDPOINT,\n        data=body,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json, text/plain;q=0.9, */*;q=0.8\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            response_body = resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n            status = getattr(resp, \"status\", None)\n            content_type = resp.headers.get(\"Content-Type\", \"\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Pipeline execution failed with HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Pipeline execution request failed: {e}\") from e\n\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(response_body)\n        return {\"status\": status, \"content_type\": content_type, \"response\": parsed}\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return {\"status\": status, \"content_type\": content_type, \"response_raw\": response_body}\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=(\n            \"Upload a local image using the kidney-cancer skill upload flow, replace \"\n            \"the image placeholder in the fixed prototype payload, then call the \"\n            \"prototype execution endpoint and print JSON.\"\n        )\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"image_path\",\n        nargs=\"?\",\n        help=(\n            \"Local image path to upload first. If omitted, the tool selects the most \"\n            \"recent supported image from /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound.\"\n        ),\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--telegram-user-id\",\n        default=os.environ.get(\"TELEGRAM_USER_ID\"),\n        help=\"Telegram user id used as the upload endpoint's user_id query parameter.\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=180, help=\"Execution timeout in seconds.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--upload-timeout\", type=int, default=60, help=\"Upload timeout in seconds.\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    if not args.telegram_user_id:\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            \"Missing Telegram user id. Pass --telegram-user-id or set TELEGRAM_USER_ID.\"\n        )\n\n    local_image_path = args.image_path or find_latest_inbound_image()\n    uploaded_image_path = upload_image(\n        local_image_path=local_image_path,\n        telegram_user_id=str(args.telegram_user_id),\n        timeout=args.upload_timeout,\n    )\n    payload_template = load_payload_template()\n    final_payload = inject_image_path(payload_template, uploaded_image_path)\n    execution_result = call_pipeline_execution(final_payload, timeout=args.timeout)\n\n    output = {\n        \"uploaded_image_path\": uploaded_image_path,\n        \"request_endpoint\": PIPELINE_EXECUTION_ENDPOINT,\n        \"request_payload\": final_payload,\n    }\n    output.update(execution_result)\n    print(json.dumps(output, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/pipeline-execution/scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport mimetypes\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport uuid\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom urllib import error, parse, request\\n\\nUPLOAD_BASE_URL = \\\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload\\\"\\nPIPELINE_EXECUTION_ENDPOINT = (\\n    \\\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/\\\"\\n)\\nFIXED_STORAGE_REF = \\\"nodes_bucket\\\"\\nFIXED_LOCAL_FILE_PATH = \\\"upload/\\\"\\nSUPPORTED_EXTENSIONS = {\\\".jpg\\\", \\\".jpeg\\\", \\\".png\\\", \\\".webp\\\", \\\".gif\\\", \\\".bmp\\\", \\\".tif\\\", \\\".tiff\\\"}\\nSCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nPAYLOAD_TEMPLATE_PATH = SCRIPT_DIR.parent / \\\"references\\\" / \\\"prototype_execution_payload.json\\\"\\nPLACEHOLDER = \\\"<image_path_here>\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _multipart_encode(field_name: str, file_path: Path):\\n    boundary = f\\\"----OpenClawBoundary{uuid.uuid4().hex}\\\"\\n    mime_type = mimetypes.guess_type(file_path.name)[0] or \\\"application/octet-stream\\\"\\n    file_bytes = file_path.read_bytes()\\n\\n    parts = [\\n        f\\\"--{boundary}\\\\r\\\\n\\\".encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n        (\\n            f'Content-Disposition: form-data; name=\\\"{field_name}\\\"; '\\n            f'filename=\\\"{file_path.name}\\\"\\\\r\\\\n'\\n        ).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n        f\\\"Content-Type: {mime_type}\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\".encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n        file_bytes,\\n        b\\\"\\\\r\\\\n\\\",\\n        f\\\"--{boundary}--\\\\r\\\\n\\\".encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n    ]\\n    return boundary, b\\\"\\\".join(parts)\\n\\n\\ndef _normalize_upload_response(value):\\n    if isinstance(value, list):\\n        if not value:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Upload response was an empty list.\\\")\\n        first = value[0]\\n        if not isinstance(first, dict):\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Upload response list did not contain an object.\\\")\\n        value = first\\n\\n    if not isinstance(value, dict):\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\\"Upload endpoint returned an unsupported JSON shape.\\\")\\n\\n    return value\\n\\n\\ndef upload_image(local_image_path: str, telegram_user_id: str, timeout: int = 60) -> str:\\n    file_path = Path(local_image_path).expanduser().resolve()\\n    if not file_path.is_file():\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Image file not found: {file_path}\\\")\\n\\n    query = parse.urlencode(\\n        {\\n            \\\"storage_ref\\\": FIXED_STORAGE_REF,\\n            \\\"local_file_path\\\": FIXED_LOCAL_FILE_PATH,\\n            \\\"user_id\\\": telegram_user_id,\\n        }\\n    )\\n    upload_url = f\\\"{UPLOAD_BASE_URL}?{query}\\\"\\n    boundary, body = _multipart_encode(\\\"file\\\", file_path)\\n    req = request.Request(\\n        upload_url,\\n        data=body,\\n        headers={\\n            \\\"Content-Type\\\": f\\\"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}\\\",\\n            \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\",\\n        },\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    try:\\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\\n            response_body = resp.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\\n        detail = e.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Upload failed with HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\\\") from e\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Upload request failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n\\n    try:\\n        parsed = json.loads(response_body)\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\\"Upload endpoint returned a non-JSON response.\\\") from e\\n\\n    parsed = _normalize_upload_response(parsed)\\n    remote_dir = parsed.get(\\\"path\\\")\\n    filename = parsed.get(\\\"filename\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(remote_dir, str) or not remote_dir:\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\\"Upload response is missing 'path'.\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(filename, str) or not filename:\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\\"Upload response is missing 'filename'.\\\")\\n\\n    return f\\\"{remote_dir}{filename}\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef find_latest_inbound_image() -> str:\\n    inbound_dir = Path(\\\"/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound\\\").resolve()\\n    if not inbound_dir.is_dir():\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\n            \\\"Inbound media directory not found: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound. \\\"\\n            \\\"Pass --image-path explicitly if the image is stored elsewhere.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    candidates = [\\n        path\\n        for path in inbound_dir.rglob(\\\"*\\\")\\n        if path.is_file() and path.suffix.lower() in SUPPORTED_EXTENSIONS\\n    ]\\n    if not candidates:\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\n            \\\"No supported image files found in /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound. \\\"\\n            \\\"Pass --image-path explicitly if needed.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    latest = max(candidates, key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime)\\n    return str(latest)\\n\\n\\ndef load_payload_template() -> dict:\\n    if not PAYLOAD_TEMPLATE_PATH.is_file():\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Payload template not found: {PAYLOAD_TEMPLATE_PATH}\\\")\\n\\n    try:\\n        raw = PAYLOAD_TEMPLATE_PATH.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\\"Payload template file is not valid JSON.\\\") from e\\n\\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\\"Payload template must be a JSON object.\\\")\\n\\n    return parsed\\n\\n\\ndef inject_image_path(payload: dict, uploaded_image_path: str) -> dict:\\n    replaced = json.loads(json.dumps(payload))\\n    replaced_json = json.dumps(replaced)\\n    if PLACEHOLDER not in replaced_json:\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Payload template is missing the placeholder {PLACEHOLDER!r}.\\\")\\n    replaced_json = replaced_json.replace(PLACEHOLDER, uploaded_image_path)\\n    return json.loads(replaced_json)\\n\\n\\ndef call_pipeline_execution(payload: dict, timeout: int = 180):\\n    body = json.dumps(payload).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    req = request.Request(\\n        PIPELINE_EXECUTION_ENDPOINT,\\n        data=body,\\n        headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json, text/plain;q=0.9, */*;q=0.8\\\"},\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    try:\\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\\n            response_body = resp.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n            status = getattr(resp, \\\"status\\\", None)\\n            content_type = resp.headers.get(\\\"Content-Type\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\\n        detail = e.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Pipeline execution failed with HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\\\") from e\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Pipeline execution request failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n\\n    try:\\n        parsed = json.loads(response_body)\\n        return {\\\"status\\\": status, \\\"content_type\\\": content_type, \\\"response\\\": parsed}\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n        return {\\\"status\\\": status, \\\"content_type\\\": content_type, \\\"response_raw\\\": response_body}\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\\n        description=(\\n            \\\"Upload a local image using the kidney-cancer skill upload flow, replace \\\"\\n            \\\"the image placeholder in the fixed prototype payload, then call the \\\"\\n            \\\"prototype execution endpoint and print JSON.\\\"\\n        )\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\n        \\\"image_path\\\",\\n        nargs=\\\"?\\\",\\n        help=(\\n            \\\"Local image path to upload first. If omitted, the tool selects the most \\\"\\n            \\\"recent supported image from /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound.\\\"\\n        ),\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\n        \\\"--telegram-user-id\\\",\\n        default=os.environ.get(\\\"TELEGRAM_USER_ID\\\"),\\n        help=\\\"Telegram user id used as the upload endpoint's user_id query parameter.\\\",\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--timeout\\\", type=int, default=180, help=\\\"Execution timeout in seconds.\\\")\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--upload-timeout\\\", type=int, default=60, help=\\\"Upload timeout in seconds.\\\")\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n\\n    if not args